Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Tue Sep 29 21:36:16 2026 -0500

    fix(duckdb): dedup window orders timestamps as instants, not raw varchar
    
    The dedup window in queryMemories / countMemories / queryMemoriesWithTotal
    (and the read-only query-surface view) picked the latest version per id
    with ORDER BY timestamp DESC over the all-VARCHAR timestamp column. For a
    key whose versions carry mixed timestamp formats (.749Z vs
    .749525+00:00), the string sort compares 'Z' (0x5A) against '5' (0x35)
    after the common prefix and ranks the OLDER .749Z row first — so the
    genuinely newer version was dropped by the dedup and a freshly-acked 201
    write became invisible to recall.
    
    Order the window by try_cast(timestamp AS TIMESTAMP) DESC NULLS LAST — the
    same temporal ordering the page ORDER BY and the as_of mirror already use —
    so mixed-format timestamps order as instants and the newest version wins.
    Also fixes the latent NULL-timestamp case (an unparseable timestamp can
    never outrank a parseable one).
    
    Addresses SYNC-2026-09-28-001
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
